PTP Daemon Version 2 Build and Installation Instructions

Updated: February 8, 2026 (CMake build system)

The PTP Daemon is known to work on FreeBSD, NetBSD, OpenBSD,
OpenSolaris and its derivatives, macOS and Linux systems.

REQUIREMENTS
============

You will need the following tools and libraries to build ptpd2:

1. CMake 3.15 or later - required

2. C compiler (GCC, Clang, MSVC) - required

3. PCAP libraries (libpcap/bpf) and development headers
   (optional but recommended) - required for Ethernet transport
   and generally recommended for message performance

4. SNMP libraries (optional) - enables SNMP monitoring support
   (net-snmp on Linux/Unix, or compatible)

QUICK START
===========

1. cd into the root of the tree (where this file resides)

2. Configure and build:

   cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
   cmake --build build

   Binary will be in: build/src/ptpd2

3. Install (optional):

   sudo cmake --install build --prefix /usr/local

CONFIGURATION OPTIONS
=====================

CMake provides many configuration options. Common examples:

* Disable statistics (lower CPU/RAM usage):
  cmake -B build -DENABLE_STATISTICS=OFF

* Build slave-only version:
  cmake -B build -DENABLE_SLAVE_ONLY=ON

* Disable POSIX timers (use interval timers):
  cmake -B build -DENABLE_POSIX_TIMERS=OFF

* Set maximum unicast destinations:
  cmake -B build -DMAX_UNICAST_DESTINATIONS=256

* Enable runtime debug messages:
  cmake -B build -DENABLE_RUNTIME_DEBUG=ON

* Set debug level (basic, medium, all):
  cmake -B build -DDEBUG_LEVEL=all

For complete list of options, see:
- README.cmake.md (comprehensive build guide)
- CONFIGURATION.md (technical details for all 12 options)

Or run: cmake -B build -LH

TESTING
=======

1. Read the manual pages ptpd2(8) and ptpd2.conf(5). The man pages
   are the most complete source of configuration information.
   
2. ptpd2 provides extensive help:
   - Run: ptpd2 --help (short help)
   - Run: ptpd2 --long-help (all settings)
   - Run: ptpd2 -e [key:setting] (single setting help)

3. Update resources/test/client-e2e-socket.conf so that its
   "ptpengine:interface = " setting points to a network interface on
   your test machine that can see PTP packets from a grandmaster.

4. Test in place: ./build/src/ptpd2 -c resources/test/client-e2e-socket.conf

5. Check the log output:
   - Event log: /var/run/ptpd2.event.log
   - Statistics: /var/run/ptpd2.stats.log
   - Status file: /var/run/ptpd2.status.log

DEVELOPMENT BUILDS
==================

For development with debug symbols:

cmake -B build-debug -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug
cmake --build build-debug

Binary with debug symbols: build-debug/src/ptpd2

Multiple build configurations can coexist:
- build-debug/ (Debug build)
- build-release/ (Release build)
- build-custom/ (Custom configuration)

See MyREADME.txt for VS Code integration and development workflows.

